  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe post option `end_units` (\"the unit the program ends in\", #596) is offered for every post: by the new Post dialog (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/post_dialog_tabs.rs`, the \"End units\" row: Leave modal / Inch (G20) / mm (G21)) and by the MCP `set_post_options`. Seven of the ten built-in and shipped mill posts ignore it without a word.\n\nThe program still ends in its own unit, so the control is left in the unit the user asked to leave behind. #596's reason for the option (\"a mm program on an inch-run control leaves the DRO and MDI in mm\") is unmet, and nothing tells the user.\n\n## Reproduction (main 4b7a6b1e, `camcraft-cli mcp`)\n\n```json\n[[\"load_machine\", {\"builtin\": \"VMC 3-axis\"}],\n [\"set_stock\", {\"box\": {\"dx\": 60, \"dy\": 40, \"dz\": 10}}],\n [\"add_tool\", {\"catalog\": \"EM-1000-4FL\"}],\n [\"add_operation\", {\"kind\": \"face\", \"tool\": \"EM-1000-4FL\", \"name\": \"F1\"}],\n [\"generate\", {}],\n [\"post\", {\"output\": \"before.nc\", \"post\": \"<post>\"}],\n [\"set_post_options\", {\"end_units\": \"inch\"}],\n [\"post\", {\"output\": \"after.nc\", \"post\": \"<post>\"}]]\n```\n\n`set_post_options` accepts the value, and both posts succeed with no warning. `diff before.nc after.nc`:\n\n| Post | Change |\n|---|---|\n| Fanuc, Haas, Siemens 840D, Heidenhain, Mazak, `doosan-dnm.cps`, `carvera.cps` | none |\n| `tormach.cps`, `grblhal.cps`, `tinyg.cps` | `G20` added just before `M30` |\n\n## Root cause (confirmed)\n\n`posting::options_value` hands the script `postOptions.EndUnits` (`\"inch\"` / `\"mm\"`). Only `tormach.cps`, `grblhal.cps` and `tinyg.cps` read it: `grep -l EndUnits assets/posts/*.cps`. Nothing refuses or notes the option for a post that does not read it.\n\nThe older Post page gates its own \"End in\" picker to the Tormach PathPilot post (`post_options::end_units_picker`). The new dialog and the MCP tool do not gate it.\n\n#757 settled the same shape for Smoothing: a post that cannot write the asked smoothing says so once (\"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN\") instead of dropping it silently.\n\n## Expected\n\nEach post either writes the asked end unit (`G20` / `G21`, or the control's own word) before the end of the program, or says once that it did not. A choice the post ignores is not offered as if it worked.\n\n## Suggested labels\n\nOutside contributors can't set labels, so these are suggestions:\n\n- `P3`: a dialog choice and an MCP option that cannot do what they say, with no word that they did nothing.\n- `effort:high`: posted G-code in seven scripts.\n- `area:post`\n- `source:agent`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
